    {
      "id": 225787,
      "name": "Eric R",
      "username": "Eric_R",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/b9bd4f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-02-27T20:00:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><strong>TL;DR</strong>: Yes, in this Scenario, you can search a land partway through a Power.</p>\n<p><strong>Longform</strong>: As the Scenario is written - \"whenever a land has 3 more more Dahan...\" -&nbsp;you may search a land even in the middle of a&nbsp;Power. This is an accident of wording; the nomenclature(*) which clearly differentiates between the two meanings&nbsp;wasn't standardized until the upcoming Jagged Earth expansion, so a variety of core-game / Branch &amp; Claw materials don't use it consistently. But here, it&nbsp;matches the original design intent(**), so in this case it's a fortunate accident rather than an \"ah, crud\" one(***).</p>\n<p><em>* = Starting with Jagged Earth, instructions that read \"When X, do Y\" can happen even during other actions, while \"After X, do Y\" holds off until after an action is finished.</em></p>\n<p><em>** = Turns are several years, so the Dahan are able to search the land while traveling through.</em></p>\n<p><em>*** = Dahan Insurrection is one of the 'ah, crud' cases: it uses \"When\", and then explicitly spells out in reminder text that what it means is \"After\".</em></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:31.265Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 5.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 18979,
      "topic_slug": "question-on-powers-long-forgotten",
      "display_username": "Eric R",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p><strong>TL;DR</strong>: Yes, in this Scenario, you can search a land partway through a Power.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Longform</strong>: As the Scenario is written - \"whenever a land has 3 more more Dahan...\" -&nbsp;you may search a land even in the middle of a&nbsp;Power. This is an accident of wording; the nomenclature(*) which clearly differentiates between the two meanings&nbsp;wasn't standardized until the upcoming Jagged Earth expansion, so a variety of core-game / Branch &amp; Claw materials don't use it consistently. But here, it&nbsp;matches the original design intent(**), so in this case it's a fortunate accident rather than an \"ah, crud\" one(***).</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>* = Starting with Jagged Earth, instructions that read \"When X, do Y\" can happen even during other actions, while \"After X, do Y\" holds off until after an action is finished.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>** = Turns are several years, so the Dahan are able to search the land while traveling through.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>*** = Dahan Insurrection is one of the 'ah, crud' cases: it uses \"When\", and then explicitly spells out in reminder text that what it means is \"After\".</em></p>",
